    "reason": "The TypeScript registers read-result and apply-result only when the in-app MCP server first asks a question (mcp-queries listen()), and nothing ever listens to bytes-result. The harness records the TypeScript side's missing listener as a thrown 'No handler registered'; Electron drops such a send, so the renderer sees nothing. The Rust side must register a handler for every send channel of the table (shell start rule) and ignores a reply nobody waits for."
